  {
    "id": "example-cover-control-cover-control-example",
    "type": "comment",
    "name": "Cover control example",
    "info": "A position cover (blind, shutter or curtain motor) owned by the cover controller. Requests go in as \"open\", \"close\", \"stop\", a position from 0 to 100, or a preset name; an automatic target sets respectManual so a person's move holds. The Zigbee2MQTT cover adapter maps to and from a Zigbee2MQTT cover: set its friendly name, and it reads the cover's state and availability from the broker and sends it the controller's commands. A button can stop the cover if it is moving and open it otherwise, and the cover's availability keeps requests from going to an offline device. Output 3 says whether the cover is moving, for other policies to react to. Here it pauses motion lighting while the cover moves, through the motion policy's pause input, which never touches the user's own enable.\n\nBefore deploying, open the \"your MQTT broker\" config node (any node's Broker setting) and set your broker's host: every node here that talks MQTT subscribes and publishes through it, with no MQTT in, MQTT out or status nodes. Give the cover controller an area and choose what it publishes to show the cover in Home Assistant.",
    "x": 170,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
